+# Implementation Plan — Dashboard UI Enhancement
+
+## Goal
+Elevate the role-based dashboard home (`src/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/page.tsx`) to a more
+polished, "top-level app" feel — without discarding the existing pine/saffron/paper design
+identity (Fraunces display + Inter body + JetBrains mono labels).
+
+## Scope
+In scope: `AdminHome`, `TeacherHome`, `StudentHome`, `ParentHome` and the shared `StatCard`
+component. Sidebar/TopBar are explicitly out of scope for this session.
+
+## Changes
+
+1. **`StatCard.tsx`**
+   - Add a colored icon "chip" background instead of a bare icon.
+   - Support an optional `hint` (small secondary line, e.g. "3 today") without requiring
+     fabricated trend data no API currently provides.
+   - Add subtle hover lift (`translate-y` + shadow) for interactivity.
+   - Add a staggered fade/slide-in on mount via CSS animation + inline `animationDelay`.
+
+2. **New shared `DashboardHeader` component** (`src/components/dashboard/DashboardHeader.tsx`)
+   - Time-of-day-aware greeting ("Good morning/afternoon/evening").
+   - Formatted current date.
+   - Optional right-aligned action button slot (used by AdminHome for "Mark attendance").
+   - Replaces the repeated eyebrow+h1 markup duplicated across all four home components.
+
+3. **New shared `TodayPanel` component** (`src/components/dashboard/TodayPanel.tsx`)
+   - Small "Today's sessions" list sourced from `/api/timetable` filtered to today's
+     `dayOfWeek`, reused by `AdminHome` and `TeacherHome` (both already fetch this data).
+
+4. **`AdminHome`**
+   - Use `DashboardHeader` with a "Mark attendance" quick-action button (links to
+     `/dashboard/attendance`).
+   - Add `TodayPanel` beside the "Getting started" checklist.
+   - Add skeleton loaders for stat cards (currently only ParentHome has skeletons).
+
+5. **`TeacherHome`**
+   - Use `DashboardHeader`.
+   - Add `TodayPanel`.
+   - Add skeleton loaders matching AdminHome.
+
+6. **`StudentHome`**
+   - Use `DashboardHeader`.
+   - Add skeleton loaders matching AdminHome.
+   - (No structural change beyond header/loading — keep scope tight.)
+
+7. **`ParentHome`**
+   - Use `DashboardHeader` for consistency (visual change only, no behavior change).
+
+## Non-goals
+- No new API routes or Prisma schema changes.
+- No changes to Sidebar/TopBar.
+- No new dependencies.
+
+## Verification
+- `npm run lint` — zero errors.
+- `npm run build` — zero errors.
+- Manual check: all four roles' dashboard render without console errors (visual review only,
+  no live DB in this environment — code-level correctness verified via lint/build).
